.TH POWERSIFU 1 "23 September 2026" "PowerSifu 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
powersifu \- automate Linux desktop power profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B powersifu
.RI [ --background ]
.br
.B powersifu
.RI [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PowerSifu
is a GTK system-tray utility for power-profiles-daemon. It can select profiles
when AC power changes, run recurring weekly profile schedules, and gracefully
terminate configured same-user applications when a selected profile becomes
active.
.PP
The settings window provides General, Application Rules, and Schedules pages.
Closing the window leaves the tray process running. Use Quit in the tray menu to
stop PowerSifu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start the tray service without opening the settings window.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed PowerSifu version and exit without starting the service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/powersifu/config.json
Per-user configuration. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME environment variable is honored.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.tpluharik.PowerSifu.desktop
Per-user override for automatic login startup.
.SH SECURITY
Application rules accept exact executable names only. PowerSifu sends SIGTERM
to matching processes owned by the current user and protects core desktop
processes. It does not execute arbitrary commands or install privilege rules.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR powerprofilesctl (1),
.BR power-profiles-daemon (8)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/tpluharik/powersifu/issues.
